course: dictionary
lesson: 11630
title: Digging up the past
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Archaeological is a long word, but it has a clue inside it: archaeology. Archaeology is the study of the past by digging up old objects, buildings and bones. So something archaeological is connected with that digging and studying.
explain: «The archaeological dig uncovered pots that were over two thousand years old.» The words dig and uncovered are clues that the word is about digging in the ground. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the dig about the past uncovered pots" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: «Scientists found bones at the archaeological site.» A site is a place, so an archaeological site is a place where people dig up the past. «The archaeological evidence showed that people once farmed here.» Evidence means clues, so these are clues from the past that prove people lived and farmed there.
fact: Archaeological means about archaeology, the study of the past through old objects, buildings and bones.
fact: Archaeological is an adjective: it describes a noun such as dig, site or evidence.
fact: Useful phrases are «archaeological site», «archaeological dig» and «archaeological evidence».
fact: In the US the spelling is «archeological», without the first a.
exercise: «The archaeological dig uncovered pots that were over two thousand years old.» What does archaeological tell you about the dig? | *It is about digging up old objects |  | It is about cooking dinner outdoors | It is about the study of the past | It is about building a new road
exercise: Ella says archaeology sounds hard. What does archaeology mean? | The study of stars and planets | *The study of the past by digging up old objects, buildings and bones | Cooking food from long ago | The making of old cars
exercise: «Scientists found bones at the archaeological site.» Which word tells you the site is about the study of the past? | found | *archaeological | Scientists | bones
test: Which of these is an archaeological find? | A bicycle left in the rain | A new phone bought from a shop | A cake baked this morning | *A broken pot dug up from the ground that is two thousand years old
test: «The archaeological evidence showed that people once farmed here.» What does evidence mean? | A long, boring book | A type of farm animal | Music played at a party | *Clues that prove something
exam: Which sentence uses archaeological correctly? | The archaeological rain fell all afternoon | *The team began an archaeological dig to find old coins from the Romans | My archaeological bedroom is painted blue | The team sat down for an archaeological lunch and ate sandwiches
